cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "BioChirp: Database-first Biomedical Retrieval with MCP Integration"
message: "If you use BioChirp in research, please cite this software."
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-05-10
authors:
 - family-names: Gupta
 given-names: Abhishekh
 affiliation: "Indraprastha Institute of Information Technology Delhi (IIIT-Delhi)"
 email: abhishekh@iiitd.ac.in
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/abhi1238/biochirp"
url: "https://biochirp.iiitd.edu.in"
abstract: >-
 BioChirp is a database-first biomedical question-answering system covering
 11 curated databases (TTD, CTD, HCDT, HPO, ClinVar, Reactome, MSigDB,
 Orphanet, STRING, UniProt, and Open Targets) through a shared
 schema-grounded entity-resolution and query-planning pipeline, plus a
 live web-search fallback. It exposes an MCP server (12 tools: one per
 database plus web search) for direct use from Claude and other MCP
 clients, alongside a hosted chat interface.
keywords:
 - biomedical retrieval
 - knowledge graph
 - Model Context Protocol
 - MCP
 - Claude
 - reproducibility
 - federated databases
 - drug discovery
 - rare disease
